# docs/obsidian/ is its own independent git repo (see docs/obsidian/.git) — the
# vault used to live untracked-as-its-own-repo inside this repo, so the
# obsidian-git plugin's auto-commit walked up to THIS .git and swept up
# in-progress code changes. Kept fully out of Sterling's tracking now.
docs/obsidian/


# ── kitelake: offline Kite data lake ────────────────────────────────────────
# Bulk market data lives OUTSIDE the repo (/mnt/OS/SterlingDataLake, 74 GB free)
# because "/" has ~5 GB free. `kite-data` is a symlink to it.
kite-data
.venv-kitelake/
kitelake/**/__pycache__/
kitelake/.pytest_cache/

# ── never commit these ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This remote is PUBLIC. sterling_paper.db carries exchange_configs.api_key and
# exchange_configs.api_secret (plaintext — note the column is NOT *_enc), plus
# kite_accounts and truedata_credentials. Committing it publishes live credentials.
# Untracked below with `git rm --cached`, which leaves the local file untouched.
sterling_paper.db
sterling_paper.db-*
backend/sterling_paper.db
# .env holds real credentials once filled in; .env.example documents the key list.
backend/.env
.env
# tooling / scratch output
.playwright-mcp/
youtube-transcript/
# Scratch HTML written into the served public/ directory during verification
# runs. Not ignoring it means a `git add -A` from any session commits a couple
# of hundred KB of throwaway markup — and ships it as a public asset, since
# anything under public/ is served verbatim.
frontend/public/_verify/

# Third-party tool checkouts that live inside the repo.
#
# These were committed as bare gitlinks on 2026-08-17 — swept in by a `git add -A`
# during an adaptive-edge commit — and there is no .gitmodules, so they were never
# real submodules. Two consequences: they show as permanently "modified" whenever a
# tool updates itself, and a fresh clone gets five empty directories instead of
# them. Nothing in backend/app or frontend/src imports any of them.
# The remaining gitlinks (security-review, superpowers, ui-ux-pro-max-skill) are
# removed from the index in the same change that added this ignore — CI checkout
# otherwise fails `git submodule foreach` with "No url found in .gitmodules".
awesome-claude-code/
claude-mem/
code-review/
frontend-design/
skills/
security-review/
superpowers/
ui-ux-pro-max-skill/
